# Onboarding doc - mdshare sync

Master copy: `novopay-platform-creditcard-management/docs/guides/product-onboarding.md` (GitHub `trusttai/trustt-platform-creditcard-management`). Edit on a `ddp-fea-*` branch off `origin/ddp-prod`, PR to `ddp-prod`. Same process for complaint: `docs/guides/complaint-onboarding.md` in `trustt-platform-complaint-mgmt`, branch `ddp-fea-complaint-onboarding-doc`.

mdshare copy (published view): id `6abd71df5c3812e8ca51ab39` - [link](https://mdshare.trustt.com/md/s/7NmufeEoyqRx) (personal workspace). Complaint: [link](https://mdshare.trustt.com/md/s/cppxyk87-IHN).

## Do

- Edit the repo file on the existing onboarding feature branch. PR to `ddp-prod` with `[PROD]` in the title.
- Put the **full file** in the PR description under **Rendered preview of the guide** so reviewers read it rendered (`gh pr create` / `gh pr edit <n> --body-file`).
- Refresh the **Source** line (prod branch + date) when content is re-derived from prod code. GitHub blob link must point at `ddp-prod`, not `master` or `ddp-prod-master`.
- Run the joiner loop from the `onboarding-doc` skill until that read is only Good.
- **After the PR is merged**, call mdshare `update_doc` with the **full** new file content (not a diff), then tell the user the share link still shows the old published version until they press **Publish**.
- An unpublished draft left by this same sync is fine to overwrite. If `update_doc` returns `DRAFT_DIRTY` (another user's edits), stop and tell the user - do not overwrite someone else's draft.
- Keep the title unless the user asks to rename it. CC tags: `onboarding`, `cc`, `loc`, `aoc`, `eso`, `product`, `qa`.
- Keep the layout: **Start here** (one-minute summary + per-role reading path), **Part A** (understand the product), **Part B** (reference). When sections move or are added, update the Contents and the reading-path section numbers and any `see N` cross references.

## Do not

- Do not call mdshare `update_doc` / `create_doc` while the PR is still open. Repo review first, mdshare only after merge.
- Do not create a new mdshare doc for an edit (no duplicates).
- Do not edit the mdshare copy without also editing the repo file.
- Do not keep or recreate a Desktop-level copy (`Desktop/novopay/docs/PRODUCT_ONBOARDING_CC_LOC_AOC.md` was retired).
- Style stays: visual first (mermaid + tables), minimal text, no code references, ASCII hyphens only.
